> I have a reather urgent need for a feature in Debian alpha, that
> currently doesn't work. It is the xdm login that is causing me
> a lot of grief. I am sure it will be fixed in the next version
> of the Debian xfree packages, but I'm in too much of a hurry to
> get it fixed. I hope someone can help me to get a temporary
> solution at least.

Hmm, it would appear that the i386 version of xdm statically links 
libXdmGreet.so, whereas the alpha version (and presumably others) does 
not. I'll look at it and possibly do a non-maintaner upload of X for the 
alpha with a libXdmGreet.so. Meanwhile, you can find it on 
ftp.netg.se:/pub/Linux/alpha/libxdmgreet.tar.gz - untar it in 
/usr/X11R6/lib/X11/xdm and things will hopefully work. (it's for 3.3.2, 
but it will probably work with 3.3.1 as well. 3.3.2 is available there as 
well, should you need it.)

Regards,
/Anders

